        body: 'A message carries no tone. The reader supplies it, usually from their own mood, their history with you, and the last thing you said. That is why "fine" can start a fight and why the same line reads warm to one person and cold to another. The fix is not to add exclamation marks until it feels friendly \u2014 it is to remove the two things readers use to guess a tone: ambiguity about what you want, and ambiguity about how you feel about them. Name the ask. Name the warmth. "Can you send the file by Thursday? No rush if it slips to Friday \u2014 I just need to know which."',
