        why: "Long sentences are where confidence goes to die. When a sentence runs past your lung capacity you have two bad options: push out the last words on empty air, which sounds strained and drops in pitch, or inhale mid-thought, which fractures the meaning. Both read to a listener as uncertainty. Speaking in short chunks \u2014 the UltraSpeaking idea of verse rather than prose \u2014 gives you a rhythmic floor to stand on and gives the listener time to absorb each idea.",
