        headline: "The voice has dials",
        why: 'Most people speak at a single setting. Same pitch, same pace, same volume, whether they are telling a joke or delivering bad news. That flatness is what listeners describe as "boring" or, worse, "reading" \u2014 and it has nothing to do with vocabulary. Delivery is a mixing desk with five dials: pitch, pace, pause, projection, tone. The reason to learn them as dials is that you can move one deliberately before a key sentence instead of hoping variety happens to you.',
