          `And the recoverable failure: if you forget a name, do not bluff and do not stack apologies. "I'm not going to pretend \u2014 your name has left the building. But I remember the project you were fighting for." One line of honesty plus a specific memory is more charming than a lucky recall, because it shows the relationship matters more than your record.`
