        thesis: "Speaking to a room is not conversation with more people in it. Conversation is a loop you adjust inside; a talk is a one-way transmission with a delay, and the audience gives you almost no signal until it is over. That changes the whole craft: you cannot read the room in real time, so you have to design the talk so it works without feedback \u2014 one idea, stated early, made concrete, and closed before it wears out. Nerves do not disappear; they get spent on preparation instead of performance.",
